# Copy this file to candid.env (NOT candid.env.example) next to it, fill in
# real values, and lock down its permissions:
#
#   cp candid.env.example candid.env
#   chmod 600 candid.env
#
# candid.env is read by run.sh at startup. Never commit the real candid.env
# to source control or share it outside the people who administer this
# server — SECRET_KEY in particular should be treated like a password.

# Required. Generate one with:
#   python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
SECRET_KEY=

# Optional. Enables real AI rewording via Claude instead of the built-in
# heuristic fallback. Leave blank to skip it.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Only change these if the defaults ("09:00,21:00" UTC, 4-hour
# minimum delay, 20-minute jitter) don't fit your team's timezone/rhythm.
# See the README's "Delivery timing protection" section before changing.
# FEEDBACK_RELEASE_WINDOWS=09:00,21:00
# FEEDBACK_MIN_DELAY_HOURS=4
# FEEDBACK_RELEASE_JITTER_MINUTES=20
